 75BR c  {+28}Si beam produced at E=115 MeV by the 15UD Pelletron at the        
 75BR2c  Inter University Accelerator Centre in New Delhi. The |g's             
 75BR3c  were detected using the                                                
 75BR3c  Gamma Detector Array (GDA), consisting of 12 HPGe detectors            
 75BR4c  (at 51, 98 and 144 angle with the beam axis) with a 14 element BGO     
 75BR5c  multiplicity filter. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g- coincidence, lifetimes   
 75BR6c  using the Doppler shift attenuation method.                            
 75BR cG $2009Mu16 extract B(E2) values for |DJ=2, E2 transitions in their      
 75BR2cG Table 1, but the evaluators cannot reproduce some of their values      
 75BR3cG using their lifetimes and gamma-branching ratios from the Adopted      
 75BR4cG dataset. It is possible that 2009Mu16 used a different set of          
 75BR5cG gamma-branching ratios.                                                
